1
00:00:03,540 --> 00:00:06,400
(Get ready, wake your psyche up, MOB!)

2
00:00:06,400 --> 00:00:09,210
(Get ready, dig your anger up, MOB!)

3
00:00:09,210 --> 00:00:12,060
(Get ready, wake your psyche up, MOB!)

4
00:00:12,060 --> 00:00:13,120
(Get ready!)

5
00:00:14,020 --> 00:00:18,710
Coming down, could you fill your satisfaction?

6
00:00:19,770 --> 00:00:24,450
You're a MOB. Can't you feel your own frustration?

7
00:00:25,480 --> 00:00:30,200
Coming down, could you fill your satisfaction?

8
00:00:31,220 --> 00:00:34,760
You're a MOB. What do you want to be?

9
00:00:34,760 --> 00:00:41,300
Wear your overflowing emotions on your sleeve and break it down.

10
00:00:42,520 --> 00:00:46,200
What do you see once you go beyond your limits?

11
00:00:46,200 --> 00:00:49,180
(99.9! 99.9!)

12
00:00:49,180 --> 00:00:52,060
The mysterious percentage.

13
00:00:53,740 --> 00:00:56,530
Cryin' my life, cryin' my psyche,

14
00:00:56,530 --> 00:00:59,480
cryin' my heart in such commonplaces!

15
00:00:59,480 --> 00:01:02,310
Is that your ideal? Is that your mind?

16
00:01:02,310 --> 00:01:05,220
It all begins when it hits 100.

17
00:01:05,220 --> 00:01:08,010
The MOB is alive. The MOB is high.

18
00:01:08,010 --> 00:01:10,900
The MOB is staying frustrated, aren't you?

19
00:01:10,900 --> 00:01:15,290
Is that your ideal? Is that your mind? Right now...

20
00:01:16,610 --> 00:01:17,830
Your life is your own.

21
00:01:17,830 --> 00:01:20,600
(Get ready, wake your psyche up, MOB!)

22
00:01:20,270 --> 00:01:25,110
Mob Psycho

23
00:01:20,600 --> 00:01:23,490
(Get ready, dig your anger up, MOB!)

24
00:01:23,490 --> 00:01:26,360
(Get ready, wake your psyche up, MOB!)

25
00:01:26,360 --> 00:01:27,670
(Get ready!)

26
00:01:29,980 --> 00:01:33,980
The Battle for Social Rehabilitation
~Friendship~

27
00:01:34,560 --> 00:01:37,990
Leave. I don't want you to get hurt.

28
00:01:38,790 --> 00:01:41,190
You can take this guy back with you, too.

29
00:01:41,190 --> 00:01:42,980
He's supposed to be a hostage,

30
00:01:42,980 --> 00:01:44,480
but I feel bad for him.

31
00:01:44,480 --> 00:01:46,710
Oh, it's the prime minister guy.

32
00:01:46,710 --> 00:01:49,290
What? You're the prime minister?!

33
00:01:49,830 --> 00:01:51,960
I-I'm free to go?

34
00:01:51,960 --> 00:01:52,980
Go right ahead.

35
00:01:54,610 --> 00:01:58,010
Holy cow... I just talked
to the prime minister!

36
00:01:58,240 --> 00:02:01,470
You're part of the group that abducted him,
and you had no idea?

37
00:02:01,470 --> 00:02:03,820
Well, you know, I don't watch TV.

38
00:02:03,820 --> 00:02:08,220
I see. So the public thinks
we're the bad guys.

39
00:02:08,220 --> 00:02:11,900
But you are, though. Look at
how much damage you've done to the city.

40
00:02:12,090 --> 00:02:17,030
It's fine. The president said that
most people had already evacuated.

41
00:02:17,030 --> 00:02:17,740
President?

42
00:02:18,120 --> 00:02:20,500
The person who hired me.

43
00:02:20,500 --> 00:02:24,950
He rescued me from
the hellhole that was my life.

44
00:02:24,950 --> 00:02:26,040
3 Years Ago

45
00:02:26,040 --> 00:02:27,330
Serizawa Katsuya
27 years old

46
00:02:31,040 --> 00:02:34,880
It's filthy in here. Why have you
been a shut-in for fifteen years?

47
00:02:35,910 --> 00:02:37,050
Who're you?

48
00:02:37,320 --> 00:02:39,550
My name is Suzuki.

49
00:02:39,550 --> 00:02:42,260
Your mother asked me to help you.

50
00:02:42,600 --> 00:02:44,830
Another counselor?

51
00:02:44,830 --> 00:02:48,780
Just know that if you get any closer,
you'll get hurt.

52
00:02:48,780 --> 00:02:50,350
I'm not normal.

53
00:02:50,590 --> 00:02:53,350
I hear that you're an esper.

54
00:02:53,350 --> 00:02:55,480
I understand how you feel.

55
00:02:55,480 --> 00:02:57,560
Yeah, no. Go away.

56
00:02:57,560 --> 00:03:02,000
Why? Why don't you tell me
how you're feeling?

57
00:03:02,350 --> 00:03:05,020
No... Don't say anything else.

58
00:03:05,020 --> 00:03:07,300
Please, I'm begging you. Don't annoy me.

59
00:03:07,300 --> 00:03:09,110
It must be hard...

60
00:03:09,110 --> 00:03:12,300
not being able to make friends
because people find your powers creepy.

61
00:03:11,870 --> 00:03:14,840
Potato Chips

62
00:03:11,870 --> 00:03:14,840
Yeet Tea

63
00:03:12,300 --> 00:03:14,840
Stop. Don't act like you know how I feel.

64
00:03:15,180 --> 00:03:16,920
Go away! Just go away!

65
00:03:16,920 --> 00:03:20,830
You must've been bullied
out of your place in society.

66
00:03:23,260 --> 00:03:24,430
Get out!

67
00:03:28,030 --> 00:03:30,430
I'm an esper too, you see.

68
00:03:30,630 --> 00:03:32,810
Come with me.

69
00:03:33,380 --> 00:03:36,940
B-But I get dizzy whenever I leave my room.

70
00:03:39,560 --> 00:03:41,610
It was raining outside.

71
00:03:41,850 --> 00:03:44,400
This umbrella is for you.

72
00:03:44,400 --> 00:03:47,830
Just imagine that when you're under
this umbrella, you're in your room.

73
00:03:48,220 --> 00:03:52,380
Don't worry. You'll be fine if you're with me.

74
00:03:52,380 --> 00:03:54,980
I'll show you how to use your powers.

75
00:03:56,000 --> 00:03:59,510
After that, I became an
upper echelon employee of Claw

76
00:03:59,510 --> 00:04:01,940
and regained my place in society.

77
00:04:01,940 --> 00:04:03,520
That's weird.

78
00:04:03,520 --> 00:04:04,220
Huh?

79
00:04:04,550 --> 00:04:07,810
Even I can tell that's all kinds of wrong.

80
00:04:08,200 --> 00:04:11,060
Aren't you basically just being used?

81
00:04:12,130 --> 00:04:13,890
Look who's talking!

82
00:04:14,080 --> 00:04:17,060
What a horrible thing to say...

83
00:04:17,340 --> 00:04:18,610
You're the one who's horrible.

84
00:04:19,290 --> 00:04:23,200
If this is what you were going to do,
you should've just stayed a shut-in.

85
00:04:23,580 --> 00:04:26,020
Can't you picture the faces of
the people impacted by this?

86
00:04:26,530 --> 00:04:31,700
The president said that world domination
always involved certain sacrifices.

87
00:04:31,960 --> 00:04:33,870
Do you believe that, too?

88
00:04:34,220 --> 00:04:37,580
Hey... could you leave?

89
00:04:38,030 --> 00:04:42,150
Serizawa-san, you chose
the wrong person to follow.

90
00:04:48,040 --> 00:04:49,330
You okay?

91
00:04:49,330 --> 00:04:50,470
That umbrella...

92
00:04:50,470 --> 00:04:53,560
Yeah, it's shrouded in some insane power.

93
00:04:53,850 --> 00:04:57,690
I can relax when I'm under this umbrella.

94
00:04:58,030 --> 00:04:59,990
If we can take his umbrella...

95
00:04:59,990 --> 00:05:01,900
He'll lose his strength.

96
00:05:14,640 --> 00:05:17,360
Trying to immobilize me...
isn't going to work!

97
00:05:17,940 --> 00:05:18,580
Ow...

98
00:05:19,770 --> 00:05:22,050
Oh, sorry. Are you okay?

99
00:05:22,920 --> 00:05:24,010
Wait, you were faking?

100
00:05:24,800 --> 00:05:25,880
Now, Dimple!

101
00:05:25,880 --> 00:05:27,130
You got it!

102
00:05:30,770 --> 00:05:31,970
Oh, shit!

103
00:05:34,630 --> 00:05:38,070
He explodes after only a second
without his umbrella?

104
00:05:38,070 --> 00:05:40,310
He must be incredibly anxious.

105
00:05:40,830 --> 00:05:42,860
He finally found someone
who understood him.

106
00:05:42,860 --> 00:05:44,530
He had no choice but to follow him.

107
00:05:45,390 --> 00:05:49,260
He never stood a chance against someone
who used that to their advantage.

108
00:05:50,190 --> 00:05:51,560
I have to tell him.

109
00:05:52,120 --> 00:05:55,880
That president of yours
didn't give you peace.

110
00:05:55,880 --> 00:05:58,940
He gave you the idea that
you can't live on your own

111
00:05:58,940 --> 00:06:00,750
and chained you to the organization.

112
00:06:02,130 --> 00:06:03,710
Are you a counselor?

113
00:06:04,100 --> 00:06:06,230
You can't reintegrate into society this way.

114
00:06:06,230 --> 00:06:09,680
If anything, at this rate,
you'll never be able to return.

115
00:06:10,170 --> 00:06:13,420
Like a kid who still has his whole future
ahead of him knows how I feel.

116
00:06:13,850 --> 00:06:17,430
Then tell me... What the hell
am I supposed to do?!

117
00:06:17,740 --> 00:06:20,600
No one understood this power
I was born with!

118
00:06:20,790 --> 00:06:24,090
People thought I was creepy,
so I'd lose control and cause people trouble!

119
00:06:24,090 --> 00:06:26,900
And because of that,
I'd get scorned and lose control again!

120
00:06:26,900 --> 00:06:29,310
I even accidentally sent
my mother flying before!

121
00:06:29,310 --> 00:06:32,350
I never had any idea
when I might lose control!

122
00:06:33,170 --> 00:06:36,050
I couldn't even talk to anyone...

123
00:06:36,700 --> 00:06:38,340
I just...

124
00:06:39,300 --> 00:06:41,900
I dunno... I just wanted...

125
00:06:43,000 --> 00:06:46,330
I just wanted friends.

126
00:06:49,250 --> 00:06:51,750
I have friends here.

127
00:06:51,750 --> 00:06:53,760
Espers just like me!

128
00:06:54,000 --> 00:06:55,800
You'd never understand!

129
00:06:59,640 --> 00:07:02,810
Of course I understand.
They aren't your friends.

130
00:07:03,820 --> 00:07:05,730
I actually have friends.

131
00:07:06,300 --> 00:07:07,920
That's how I know.

132
00:07:07,920 --> 00:07:09,740
They aren't your friends.

133
00:07:09,980 --> 00:07:13,490
Stop... Stop saying that over and over!

134
00:07:14,490 --> 00:07:17,330
This isn't good, Shigeo!
That's an insane amount of energy!

135
00:07:17,490 --> 00:07:20,770
I won't let you go any further!
Those are the president's orders!

136
00:07:20,770 --> 00:07:23,080
The president trusts me!

137
00:07:23,290 --> 00:07:25,960
No, it has nothing to do with trust.

138
00:07:27,630 --> 00:07:29,840
You're just being used.

139
00:07:29,840 --> 00:07:33,640
No! The president gave me a reason to live!

140
00:07:33,640 --> 00:07:36,010
But he doesn't see you as a person!

141
00:07:37,040 --> 00:07:38,430
As a person?

142
00:07:39,440 --> 00:07:41,910
You said you didn't want to hurt anyone.

143
00:07:42,380 --> 00:07:43,740
You're just like me.

144
00:07:44,070 --> 00:07:45,690
I know you realize

145
00:07:45,990 --> 00:07:47,800
that you're wrong.

146
00:07:48,200 --> 00:07:49,780
Shut up!

147
00:07:51,150 --> 00:07:54,030
In that case... I'll be your friend.

148
00:07:55,200 --> 00:07:56,120
Huh?

149
00:07:56,280 --> 00:07:57,160
Whoops...

150
00:07:57,980 --> 00:07:59,410
I shot at him.

151
00:08:01,580 --> 00:08:03,370
Shigeo!

152
00:08:03,610 --> 00:08:05,030
I even went all out!

153
00:08:10,710 --> 00:08:11,920
What?!

154
00:08:14,520 --> 00:08:17,460
You're sucking up my energy?

155
00:08:17,890 --> 00:08:20,670
I can sense what you're feeling.

156
00:08:20,670 --> 00:08:23,140
Such a sad energy...

157
00:08:23,520 --> 00:08:26,020
You turned it into your own power?

158
00:08:26,230 --> 00:08:29,150
No. You can have it back, Serizawa-san.

159
00:08:35,950 --> 00:08:37,660
What is this?

160
00:08:39,340 --> 00:08:40,160
I see...

161
00:08:40,870 --> 00:08:41,910
He's...

162
00:08:42,700 --> 00:08:44,210
He's the same as me...

163
00:08:45,620 --> 00:08:47,840
Friendship

164
00:08:49,220 --> 00:08:54,710
Now I'm going to have to recruit more
soldiers because of you and your friends.

165
00:08:54,710 --> 00:08:56,760
Stop this already, Dad.

166
00:08:57,060 --> 00:09:00,310
You can see that they aren't much help.

167
00:09:01,110 --> 00:09:04,440
Since you're my son,
I'll go ahead and tell you.

168
00:09:04,860 --> 00:09:07,400
The project of applying stress
to normal human beings

169
00:09:07,400 --> 00:09:10,250
to awaken any ESP they may have...

170
00:09:10,250 --> 00:09:12,230
It was a failure.

171
00:09:12,230 --> 00:09:14,420
Even if they did happen
to awaken to some powers,

172
00:09:14,420 --> 00:09:17,660
the most they could do was produce
some insignificant phenomenon.

173
00:09:18,080 --> 00:09:20,360
Then their powers...

174
00:09:20,360 --> 00:09:22,750
You call that an insignificant phenomenon?

175
00:09:23,570 --> 00:09:26,920
The powers they're using
like they're going out of fashion

176
00:09:26,920 --> 00:09:29,040
are my powers.

177
00:09:29,370 --> 00:09:32,850
I am able to share my power with others.

178
00:09:32,850 --> 00:09:36,810
At the same time, I am able to absorb
other people's powers as my own.

179
00:09:36,810 --> 00:09:41,310
This is my true trump card
that no one knew about.

180
00:09:41,610 --> 00:09:45,180
So you gave 600 soldiers your power?

181
00:09:45,330 --> 00:09:50,270
That's just a mere fraction of
the energy that I have accumulated.

182
00:09:50,570 --> 00:09:54,000
But that doesn't make it any less vital.

183
00:09:54,000 --> 00:09:56,990
I'll be reclaiming my energy
from those who have lost.

184
00:10:09,830 --> 00:10:11,750
I-I finally understand...

185
00:10:12,270 --> 00:10:14,060
My dad's not human.

186
00:10:14,500 --> 00:10:16,590
He's a monster made up of energy!

187
00:10:16,910 --> 00:10:19,420
Let this be a lesson, Sho.

188
00:10:19,420 --> 00:10:24,770
Only one absolute being can be
the true protagonist of this world.

189
00:10:25,190 --> 00:10:26,690
Absolute being?

190
00:10:30,230 --> 00:10:31,280
You're—

191
00:10:32,480 --> 00:10:35,990
Mob Psycho

192
00:10:35,990 --> 00:10:39,490
Mob Psycho

193
00:10:39,990 --> 00:10:41,860
You're Ritsu's older bro.

194
00:10:41,860 --> 00:10:46,200
That must mean my detonator
went off successfully.

195
00:10:46,490 --> 00:10:49,670
Are you the one who set fire to my house?

196
00:10:50,410 --> 00:10:54,120
You're probably pissed off about that,
but you should probably run.

197
00:10:54,120 --> 00:10:56,880
There's no one in this world
who can defeat him.

198
00:10:57,280 --> 00:11:01,290
I'm not mad anymore.
I'm sure you have a lot going on.

199
00:11:01,290 --> 00:11:04,210
I mean, look at what
your own father has done to you.

200
00:11:05,470 --> 00:11:06,660
Who are you?

201
00:11:07,090 --> 00:11:11,150
He's been worried about you
losing control. I can tell.

202
00:11:11,640 --> 00:11:14,530
Because my younger brother
was afraid of me, too.

203
00:11:15,090 --> 00:11:17,360
He's... changed.

204
00:11:17,630 --> 00:11:21,560
You make it sound like you know
what's going on with our family.

205
00:11:21,560 --> 00:11:26,330
Serizawa-san told me that
your son was trying to stop you.

206
00:11:26,700 --> 00:11:28,590
That your son was being beaten so badly,

207
00:11:28,590 --> 00:11:31,210
he couldn't bear to watch
and came downstairs...

208
00:11:31,910 --> 00:11:34,430
That he felt so pathetic
for not being able to step in,

209
00:11:34,430 --> 00:11:36,050
making him want to disappear.

210
00:11:36,400 --> 00:11:38,910
Serizawa lost?

211
00:11:38,910 --> 00:11:41,010
That moron. He must've gotten sloppy.

212
00:11:41,290 --> 00:11:42,520
You're wrong.

213
00:11:42,520 --> 00:11:44,150
Winning and losing

214
00:11:44,150 --> 00:11:47,220
isn't the be all and end all
in relationships between people.

215
00:11:48,650 --> 00:11:51,630
It was the president
who got me out of that room.

216
00:11:51,630 --> 00:11:52,950
I'm grateful to him.

217
00:11:53,320 --> 00:11:56,980
But why is there a need to hurt people?

218
00:11:57,340 --> 00:12:00,300
I've been too scared to think about it
so I've been running away...

219
00:12:00,300 --> 00:12:03,210
But if my happiness only came
as a result of another's tears,

220
00:12:03,210 --> 00:12:05,320
I never wanted it in the first place.

221
00:12:06,340 --> 00:12:08,750
Thank you for making me realize that.

222
00:12:11,250 --> 00:12:14,330
Apparently, trash will never be
anything more than trash.

223
00:12:15,140 --> 00:12:19,060
So be it. It's not like I ever truly
counted on others to begin with.

224
00:12:19,060 --> 00:12:22,000
Bonds with others are absolutely meaningless.

225
00:12:22,340 --> 00:12:26,070
After all, I am whole on my own.

226
00:12:26,070 --> 00:12:28,850
That's not true. Everyone...

227
00:12:29,230 --> 00:12:32,470
Everyone grows because of their
encounters with other people.

228
00:12:32,940 --> 00:12:34,980
People need other people.

229
00:12:35,360 --> 00:12:37,410
Someday, you'll need others.

230
00:12:37,780 --> 00:12:40,180
When that time comes,
you're surely going to regret things.

231
00:12:40,970 --> 00:12:44,030
So if you don't have anyone to talk to,

232
00:12:44,380 --> 00:12:45,360
I'll be there.

233
00:12:45,550 --> 00:12:47,720
You want to be a shoulder I can lean on?

234
00:12:49,080 --> 00:12:52,080
Save that kind of talk
for the weaklings of the world.

235
00:12:52,370 --> 00:12:57,290
Ritsu's bro, he can give people his energy
and steal theirs in turn.

236
00:12:57,610 --> 00:13:00,980
On top of that, he's got
a massive stock of energy himself.

237
00:13:00,980 --> 00:13:04,170
Meanwhile, I can barely even move...

238
00:13:04,940 --> 00:13:06,810
Will this help you move?

239
00:13:06,810 --> 00:13:07,740
What?

240
00:13:08,500 --> 00:13:10,470
Th-This is...

241
00:13:12,050 --> 00:13:13,680
He has the same power as me?

242
00:13:13,870 --> 00:13:14,890
Can you move?

243
00:13:14,890 --> 00:13:17,650
Y-Yeah, I can sorta stand.

244
00:13:17,920 --> 00:13:20,830
That's good. In that case,
you should evacuate, too.

245
00:13:20,830 --> 00:13:22,360
I'm going to—

246
00:13:22,570 --> 00:13:24,570
I have acknowledged you as my enemy.

247
00:13:26,200 --> 00:13:27,450
Stop!

248
00:13:28,240 --> 00:13:29,920
You stay out of this.

249
00:13:29,920 --> 00:13:32,660
He has the potential to
become my mortal enemy.

250
00:13:32,660 --> 00:13:35,870
Don't. I came here to talk.

251
00:13:36,090 --> 00:13:37,790
Give it up, Shigeo!

252
00:13:37,790 --> 00:13:39,210
You can't talk to guys like—

253
00:13:40,430 --> 00:13:41,170
You're an annoyance.

254
00:13:41,880 --> 00:13:43,380
You can disappear first.

255
00:13:43,380 --> 00:13:44,300
Dimple!

256
00:13:47,990 --> 00:13:50,930
Was it really a good idea to
let Kageyama-kun go off alone?

257
00:13:51,390 --> 00:13:55,180
I've never seen my brother
openly stamp his authority like that.

258
00:13:55,540 --> 00:13:57,860
He looked in pain to me, though.

259
00:13:58,190 --> 00:14:00,910
He's not usually the type to fight.

260
00:14:01,410 --> 00:14:03,530
What do you think, Reigen-san?

261
00:14:04,080 --> 00:14:08,430
At first glance, Mob looks pretty unreliable,
but his strength is undeniable.

262
00:14:08,430 --> 00:14:11,020
His insane telekinesis, right?

263
00:14:11,020 --> 00:14:14,570
That's just one of his qualities.

264
00:14:15,360 --> 00:14:17,250
What makes him truly great

265
00:14:17,700 --> 00:14:20,250
is his ability to tell people
exactly how he feels.

266
00:14:20,820 --> 00:14:23,840
And that speaks to their heart
far more than any niceties.

267
00:14:24,210 --> 00:14:27,810
As long as Mob's feelings can be
expressed to whoever he's facing...

268
00:14:31,930 --> 00:14:33,060
Dimple!

269
00:14:33,060 --> 00:14:34,700
What's wrong? Are you okay?

270
00:14:34,700 --> 00:14:35,640
Where's Mob?

271
00:14:36,090 --> 00:14:38,850
I'm not sure, but things look pretty grim.

272
00:14:39,260 --> 00:14:42,530
The enemy was pretty intent
on mercilessly killing Shigeo.

273
00:14:43,290 --> 00:14:45,000
Four-eyes, you got a sec?

274
00:14:47,800 --> 00:14:49,460
Talk?

275
00:14:49,460 --> 00:14:52,570
You said that bonds with others
are meaningless.

276
00:14:52,570 --> 00:14:54,490
That can't be true.

277
00:14:54,490 --> 00:14:55,620
Everyone lacks something.

278
00:14:55,620 --> 00:14:59,780
People making up for others' deficiencies
is what makes this world go around.

279
00:15:00,130 --> 00:15:02,630
All of you are so boring.

280
00:15:03,030 --> 00:15:07,500
Even among those
blessed with the gift of ESP,

281
00:15:07,500 --> 00:15:10,490
my powers far surpass them all.

282
00:15:10,490 --> 00:15:12,640
When I came to that realization,

283
00:15:13,320 --> 00:15:16,640
it appeared as though this world
could fit in the palm of my hand.

284
00:15:16,970 --> 00:15:20,880
That was when I was in middle school,
same as the two of you.

285
00:15:20,880 --> 00:15:25,370
But your mindset
puts a halt to all progress,

286
00:15:25,370 --> 00:15:30,030
leaving you living a boring life
just like the powerless.

287
00:15:30,270 --> 00:15:31,210
That's not true.

288
00:15:31,590 --> 00:15:34,910
You're the one who's stopped in place
since middle school.

289
00:15:35,610 --> 00:15:39,660
There are far more unique people
in this world than you think,

290
00:15:39,660 --> 00:15:41,290
and just as many mindsets.

291
00:15:42,010 --> 00:15:46,200
No one should be able to place a value
on another person's mindset.

292
00:15:47,060 --> 00:15:49,630
You sound like you're trying
to take the moral high ground.

293
00:15:50,030 --> 00:15:53,930
I have no need to rely on others
to make up for my deficiencies

294
00:15:53,930 --> 00:15:58,110
because I have the ability
to steal, use, and rule.

295
00:15:58,350 --> 00:16:00,310
Claw

296
00:15:59,410 --> 00:16:05,750
My goal in life is to leave
a huge mark upon this world.

297
00:16:07,450 --> 00:16:08,820
Ritsu's bro,

298
00:16:09,210 --> 00:16:11,420
don't worry about me. Just finish him off!

299
00:16:12,050 --> 00:16:18,330
Sho, I'd thought about letting you inherit
the world I was going to take over,

300
00:16:18,460 --> 00:16:21,790
but apparently you've become a failure.

301
00:16:23,970 --> 00:16:24,830
Hey.

302
00:16:28,930 --> 00:16:31,300
Are you angry on Sho's behalf?

303
00:16:32,370 --> 00:16:34,390
You truly are a child.

304
00:16:34,390 --> 00:16:35,970
Be quiet.

305
00:16:36,160 --> 00:16:39,730
This is amusing, though.
Show me everything you've got.

306
00:16:42,450 --> 00:16:44,790
This is rough...

307
00:16:54,190 --> 00:16:56,030
Stop!

308
00:16:59,100 --> 00:17:00,830
Just sit there and watch.

309
00:17:00,830 --> 00:17:02,960
This is what happens to weaklings.

310
00:17:05,750 --> 00:17:09,760
Still, you sure have some nerve
to lecture me when you're so weak.

311
00:17:10,460 --> 00:17:12,040
You can't be serious.

312
00:17:12,500 --> 00:17:13,500
Don't move.

313
00:17:15,110 --> 00:17:16,790
It's loaded, by the way.

314
00:17:18,160 --> 00:17:20,180
Sakurai's Jugan.

315
00:17:20,650 --> 00:17:23,140
You can't threaten me
with something like that.

316
00:17:23,620 --> 00:17:26,100
M-Master...

317
00:17:26,310 --> 00:17:27,810
Hey, Mob.

318
00:17:30,100 --> 00:17:32,770
I don't sense any power from you.

319
00:17:32,770 --> 00:17:35,340
You'll stay out of this
if you know what's best for you.

320
00:17:39,220 --> 00:17:42,200
Apparently, you still don't
understand how powerful I am.

321
00:17:43,440 --> 00:17:45,950
Hey, you alive, Mob?

322
00:17:47,300 --> 00:17:50,500
I don't know what I was thinking,
letting you go off alone like that.

323
00:17:50,830 --> 00:17:52,280
I think my ability to think

324
00:17:52,280 --> 00:17:54,380
was impacted by all
the unnatural things going on.

325
00:17:55,720 --> 00:17:57,430
I failed as a master.

326
00:17:57,980 --> 00:18:01,010
You did well. I'll treat you to
some takoyaki on our way home.

327
00:18:01,230 --> 00:18:02,680
Master?

328
00:18:02,680 --> 00:18:05,730
Even though you can't even see
how powerful I am?

329
00:18:06,120 --> 00:18:11,490
So you're also someone
who tricks others and steals from them.

330
00:18:11,490 --> 00:18:13,440
Well, this is ironic.

331
00:18:13,770 --> 00:18:17,850
If you ask me, you can only see
powers that can't be seen.

332
00:18:17,850 --> 00:18:19,560
I feel sorry for you.

333
00:18:19,560 --> 00:18:21,150
What's that supposed to mean?

334
00:18:21,150 --> 00:18:26,030
I'm saying ESP isn't the only
extraordinary power people can have.

335
00:18:26,030 --> 00:18:27,670
Off the top of my head,

336
00:18:27,870 --> 00:18:31,210
I can think of four ways to defeat you.

337
00:18:31,560 --> 00:18:34,170
Oh? You should give them a try, then.

338
00:18:34,460 --> 00:18:39,010
Nah, I don't feel like it.
But I do have a request...

339
00:18:40,310 --> 00:18:42,470
Will you let me join you?

340
00:18:43,030 --> 00:18:45,360
What good does that do me?

341
00:18:45,360 --> 00:18:48,430
I'd be able to easily persuade my
student who's unconscious there,

342
00:18:48,430 --> 00:18:50,610
as well as all the guys outside.

343
00:18:50,610 --> 00:18:52,940
That should be reason enough.

344
00:18:53,230 --> 00:18:56,560
Let's hear about these methods
of defeating me as well...

345
00:18:56,560 --> 00:18:58,470
If you actually have any, that is.

346
00:18:59,240 --> 00:19:03,360
I'll fill you in on some powers other
than ESP that you don't know about.

347
00:19:03,950 --> 00:19:05,290
The first power...

348
00:19:05,690 --> 00:19:09,250
The power that espers should
be extremely cautious about...

349
00:19:09,460 --> 00:19:10,460
That's...

350
00:19:10,680 --> 00:19:12,530
brute strength, you moron!

351
00:19:14,020 --> 00:19:16,980
I guess I can see how you two
are master and student.

352
00:19:16,980 --> 00:19:18,890
What a ridiculous combination.

353
00:19:19,890 --> 00:19:21,300
W-Wait! I give up!

354
00:19:21,690 --> 00:19:23,640
I'll do anything you ask.

355
00:19:23,900 --> 00:19:26,920
You have put me in an extremely foul mood.

356
00:19:25,340 --> 00:19:26,920
U-Um...

357
00:19:26,920 --> 00:19:29,060
N-N-No, wait! Let's talk about—

358
00:19:30,020 --> 00:19:30,840
Sto—

359
00:19:43,020 --> 00:19:44,640
What's going on?

360
00:19:44,950 --> 00:19:46,580
Reigen-san...

361
00:19:55,910 --> 00:19:57,360
I made it in time.

362
00:19:57,360 --> 00:20:00,920
I tried being courageous for once, President.

363
00:20:01,100 --> 00:20:04,310
Serizawa... I see that you've
completely betrayed me now.

364
00:20:04,310 --> 00:20:05,860
In that case...

365
00:20:05,860 --> 00:20:07,310
Forget it.

366
00:20:07,830 --> 00:20:10,080
That's enough talk.

367
00:20:12,480 --> 00:20:13,650
Rage

368
00:20:15,800 --> 00:20:18,230
Let me just tell you one last thing.

369
00:20:18,610 --> 00:20:21,300
Those who don't understand
the feelings of others...

370
00:20:22,420 --> 00:20:23,700
Never mind.

371
00:20:23,990 --> 00:20:26,120
Sometimes you need to be
hurt to truly understand.

372
00:20:26,890 --> 00:20:27,800
That's...

373
00:20:28,310 --> 00:20:29,370
It's Nii-san.

374
00:20:29,650 --> 00:20:31,120
Shigeo...

375
00:20:31,910 --> 00:20:33,480
Mob's lost it.

376
00:20:33,480 --> 00:20:36,540
I-Is there anything I can help with?

377
00:20:36,790 --> 00:20:40,340
Serizawa-san, take my master
and the others and evacuate.

378
00:20:40,690 --> 00:20:42,170
Punishment comes first!

379
00:20:45,410 --> 00:20:46,670
Shigeo-kun!

380
00:20:49,520 --> 00:20:50,340
That's...

381
00:20:50,340 --> 00:20:51,230
That's not good!

382
00:20:53,650 --> 00:20:54,640
Nii-san.

383
00:20:56,060 --> 00:20:57,300
Plants?

384
00:21:05,140 --> 00:21:08,730
So the boss really did cast Serizawa aside.

385
00:21:08,730 --> 00:21:09,660
Who?

386
00:21:09,950 --> 00:21:12,310
Sorry, but I owe him one.

387
00:21:12,310 --> 00:21:15,710
Don't, Minegishi! If you piss off the boss...

388
00:21:15,710 --> 00:21:17,380
So you're okay too, Hatori.

389
00:21:18,190 --> 00:21:19,550
Minegishi, eh?

390
00:21:20,760 --> 00:21:24,340
Apparently, I'm now in a situation
where anyone can betray me.

391
00:21:24,340 --> 00:21:26,300
Back to the drawing board, I suppose.

392
00:21:26,990 --> 00:21:28,050
Disappear.

393
00:21:35,730 --> 00:21:39,140
Disappear. Disappear. Disappear.

394
00:21:44,020 --> 00:21:46,200
Well, you're enthusiastic.

395
00:21:46,200 --> 00:21:47,450
Output 10%

396
00:21:52,120 --> 00:21:54,790
You're weak. Too weak.

397
00:21:55,520 --> 00:21:58,270
I'm still only using 10 percent of my powers.

398
00:21:58,270 --> 00:22:01,450
Is that your 100 percent?

399
00:22:07,870 --> 00:22:09,390
What the hell is that?

400
00:22:11,520 --> 00:22:15,560
I see. So that's what you were after.

401
00:22:15,890 --> 00:22:18,650
Now I'll be able to hit
you with everything...

402
00:22:19,230 --> 00:22:22,740
My powers... and my rage.

403
00:22:36,640 --> 00:22:41,670
I spilled a seed and lost sight of it

404
00:22:45,380 --> 00:22:50,680
I'll find it using the color it's dyed in and watch it grow

405
00:22:53,020 --> 00:22:59,150
It immediately returned to the palm of my hand

406
00:22:59,150 --> 00:23:08,720
But it's still too light and too frail to reach for the skies

407
00:23:09,780 --> 00:23:14,340
The world coldly drains away all the heat

408
00:23:14,340 --> 00:23:18,890
The bright sunshine just isn't enough

409
00:23:18,890 --> 00:23:23,280
The memories are closing off what lies ahead

410
00:23:23,280 --> 00:23:28,380
Shake off their warmth and set off into the distance

411
00:23:29,640 --> 00:23:35,140
If I let it wither, it'd be over just like that

412
00:23:35,140 --> 00:23:40,430
But my hope just doesn't fade away

413
00:23:55,640 --> 00:23:59,540
The final battle begins between an enraged
Mob and the energy demon, Suzuki.

414
00:23:59,930 --> 00:24:02,330
Don't push yourself too hard, Mob.

415
00:24:02,330 --> 00:24:04,850
Next time on Mob Psycho 100 II Episode 13:

416
00:24:04,850 --> 00:24:06,750
"Boss Fight ~The Final Light~."

417
00:24:06,750 --> 00:24:09,540
Watching the finale in real time
is an excellent decision.

418
00:24:06,960 --> 00:24:10,210
Boss Fight
~The Final Light~
